-- title:
--   Complete observed counting history jointly factorises from the residual and full IID future
-- statement:
--   When an event is measurable in the natural pullback sigma-algebra generated by the complete renewal counting history through a fixed horizon, the accepted finite-prefix representation theorem constructs its countwise representation from the interarrival prefix. The accepted countwise IID factorisation then proves the event jointly independent of residual exponential survival and every measurable event of the entire future suffix, under explicitly stated common suffix-law and exponential-tail hypotheses. This theorem provides a direct natural-filtration step.
